WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.876
- [Announcer] Icon!

00:00:01.876 --> 00:00:03.590
(epic music)

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:04.423
Legend!

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.431
All-time great!

00:00:08.431 --> 00:00:10.010
(crowd cheering)

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.320
Garth Brooks is simply put:

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.330
one of the most successful
recording artist

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.256
and performers in history.

00:00:15.256 --> 00:00:18.006
(crowd cheering)

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.500
Born in Tulsa Oklahoma,

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.250
Garth got his start singing
in dive bars and clubs

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.300
before releasing his first album in 1989.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.870
That album was just the beginning

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.140
as Garth would go on to become

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.620
the best-selling solo artist of all time

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.450
with over 148 million albums sold.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.480
His generational talent helped make Garth

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.840
the only artist in
music history to receive

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.850
seven diamond album awards

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.340
which commemorate over 10
million in sales for each album.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.810
Blending country music,
a rock and roll flare,

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.410
and captivating storytelling,

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.700
Garth is known world-wide

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.313
for his stunning live shows.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.690
A unique mix of the intimate,

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:56.880
the spectacular,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.719
and above all, an unmatched
gratitude for his fans.

00:00:59.719 --> 00:01:02.552
(emotional music)

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.380
He remains the only artist to win

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:08.170
seven CMA entertainer of the year awards

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:11.003
and he continues to sell out
shows all over the world.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.430
Garth Brooks is undeniably
a living legend.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:16.550
And the best part is,

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.880
he shows no sign of slowing down y'all.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.623
His legacy only continues to grow.

00:01:23.432 --> 00:01:26.381
(crowd cheering)

00:01:26.381 --> 00:01:27.933
- So,

00:01:27.933 --> 00:01:29.741
first of all

00:01:29.741 --> 00:01:32.640
I think that this is
the greatest idea ever

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.530
because what I'm obsessed with vinyl.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.610
And also you're like the
smartest businessman ever,

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:39.440
because you can't get your music in a rest

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.350
so this is amazing!

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.860
Because we're all gonna get it!

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:43.693
(clapping and cheering)

00:01:43.693 --> 00:01:45.135
So why did you decide
to release it on vinyl?

00:01:45.135 --> 00:01:46.110
- Well you know the weird thing was we

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:47.740
you know, we went over
and raise our babies,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.940
but when we came back,
vinyl was coming back.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.010
And you got to be kidding me, right?

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.580
And it's so cool, but then you start

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.620
to look at pieces, right?

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:56.670
So you collect vinyl,

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.503
- Yes.

00:01:57.503 --> 00:02:01.200
- You know they cost 29 bucks,
39 for a piece of vinyl!

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.033
- Yeah.

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:04.060
- So we got with a company that
had plans all over the world

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.340
and said, "make me a box if you can

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.760
where people can pick
it up for a great cost".

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.070
It doesn't cost, but Morgan
should have the whole

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.050
collection, so here it comes.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.100
All our stuff on vinyl for the first time

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.100
and I gotta tell ya,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.190
we have turn table at home

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:21.140
and I just played this album, which is

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.560
one of my dearest babies right here, but

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.750
just played it on there
and it all just comes back

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.710
to the very first time you heard it.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:28.543
- Ain't that amazing?

00:02:28.543 --> 00:02:29.376
(cheering and clapping)

00:02:29.376 --> 00:02:30.900
That's what I love about vinyl.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:31.733
- Something about it, I
don't know what it is.

00:02:31.733 --> 00:02:34.180
- I think it's so great that
you're doing it 'cause I think

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:38.180
I saw you in Vegas, your
residency and I was blown away

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:40.143
because I missed, I was telling
the audience earlier I was

00:02:40.143 --> 00:02:42.950
so poor as a kid, I
couldn't go to any concert.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:44.670
So I never got to,
everybody from school would

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.650
came back with all the
merch, and the T-shirts

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.850
it would be like, "and another
awesome concert I missed!"

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:50.950
So like, "Cool!"

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:53.060
But like, it was one of those
things when I got to see you

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:53.893
in Vegas, it was almost better

00:02:53.893 --> 00:02:55.860
in Vegas, it was almost better

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.742
because it was just you and your guitar,

00:02:57.742 --> 00:02:58.575
- Yes ma'am

00:02:58.575 --> 00:03:02.283
- and you were like, the
greatest storyteller ever.

00:03:02.283 --> 00:03:03.116
- That's really sweet.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.040
- I was captivated the entire,

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.570
I only use the word captivated
when describing Meryl Streep,

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:08.530
this is a big moment for me.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:09.363
- Wow, thank you very much.

00:03:09.363 --> 00:03:10.196
(audience laughing)

00:03:10.196 --> 00:03:11.690
- But no! I'm just saying like, I

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:12.920
was captivated the entire time!

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.340
I was looking at Reba
and Narvel over together

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.920
and I was like, "What is
happening!? He's got his guitar

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:17.753
and he's just covering all this

00:03:17.753 --> 00:03:18.747
and just telling stories about it

00:03:18.747 --> 00:03:19.940
and the songs that you love,

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.278
'cause you love covering music as well.

00:03:21.278 --> 00:03:22.111
- Yes ma'am.

00:03:22.111 --> 00:03:24.410
- It was the most amazing thing I've seen.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.140
I think you were the most talented,

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.915
down to earth, like cool guy.

00:03:27.915 --> 00:03:28.748
- Thank you.

00:03:28.748 --> 00:03:29.581
(clapping)

00:03:29.581 --> 00:03:30.414
You know what?

00:03:30.414 --> 00:03:31.600
I'm gonna send you a big ass box

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.260
of all the T-shirts and
all the merch that we had

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:34.093
during those shows,

00:03:34.093 --> 00:03:36.030
- You know what? Don't you
threaten me with a good time,

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:36.863
right Collins?

00:03:36.863 --> 00:03:37.696
- I will.

00:03:37.696 --> 00:03:38.529
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:38.529 --> 00:03:40.003
I'll send it to ya, so you can catch up.

